president reagan loved it test audiences  were puzzled by it and princess diana  was at the world premiere great scot  seeing back to the future in 1985 sure  sounds like a trip let's go back in time  some films take a while to find their  audience even movies that are later  considered classics don't always receive  a warm reception at the box office or  enjoy favorable reviews when they first  come out but not back to the future from  the start film reviewers from major  publications like the new york times and  variety all gave the movie glowing  reviews some like newsweek's jack kroll  called the film quote the smartest  sweetest funniest comedy in many summers  others like empire's adam smith praised  the screenplay an observation that would  be echoed in film classes for decades  film critic roger ebert was particularly  complimentary giving the flick three and  a half out of four stars in his review  ebert compared the film to the all-time  classic it's a wonderful life praising  the hopeful way it allowed audiences to  see their parents in a new life director  robert zemeckis also received accolades  from the legendary critic with ebert  claiming that his touch gave the film  quote charm brains and a lot of laughter  considering that the project was turned  down 40 times by multiple studios before  being made the warm critical reception  to back to the future had to be  extremely gratifying  one of the funniest moments from back to  the future came when the doc brown of  1955 asked marty who the president of  the united states was in 1985 and then  reacted with disbelief when he heard  that actor ronald reagan would become  president reagan in the future who's  president of the united states in 1985  ronald reagan ronald reagan the actor  according to his former speech writer  mark weinberg reagan who viewed the film  for the first time at camp david got a  kick out of an early scene where marty  walked by a 1955 movie theater  advertising the reagan film cattle queen  of montana when doc had his famous  exchange with marty however the mood at  camp david darkened not because of doc's  comment about reagan but because the  character then sarcastically asked i  suppose jane wyman is a first lady  wyman was reagan's first wife whom he  divorced in 1949 by 1955 he was married  to future first lady nancy reagan while  the movie completely ignored that fact  reagan didn't according to weinberg  there was a quote unspoken ban on  mentioning wyman among the reagan staff  making the film's reference to her a  very uncomfortable moment  despite his brief discomforts at the  mention of ex-wife jane wyman by doc  brown president ronald reagan became a  big fan of back to the future his speech  writer weinberg would later recall that  both ronald and nancy reagan were  impressed by michael j fox's performance  as marty mcfly this may have been  related to the fact that fox was also  playing republican teenager alex keaton  on the reagan's favorite television show  at the time family ties weinberg said  that reagan remarked about back to the  future  this was the type of movie that  hollywood should be making  six months later president reagan even  quoted back to the future in his  february 4 1986 state of the union  address encouraging the american people  to look to the skies as the limits of  their achievements reagan said as they  said in the film back to the future  where we're going  we don't need roads  zamakis ultimately chose to use a  delorean as the basis for his time  machine partly because the gull wing  doors of the car would allow a 1955  family to mistake the vehicle for an  alien spacecraft when marty crashes into  their barn although ford offered the  production team money if they made the  time machine out of a mustang co-writer  bob gale reportedly responded with quote  doc brown doesn't drive a mustang  the time machine's stylish and memorable  design earned the filmmakers praise from  the sports car's original designer john  delorean by 1982 the delorean motor  company had gone bankrupt and its  factory closed this ended delorean's  dream of creating a quote ethical sports  car thanks to back to the future however  the delorean dmc 12's image was  immortalized realizing the movie had  kept his dream alive john delorean sent  the filmmakers a fan letter thanking  them for using his car  john delorean wasn't the only fan of  back to the future that loved the car  the film fueled a major delorean  collecting craze that persists to this  day reportedly the delorean motor  company only managed to produce over 9  000 dmc 12s before the company went  bankrupt in 1982. however thanks in part  to back to the future an estimated 6 500  delorean cars are still on the road  today this is in sharp contrast to other  discontinued car models which normally  phase out of existence once they stop  being made ironically in 1984 former  delorean dealer steve lopinto claimed  the car quote doesn't have enough  mystique to become a collector's car  flash forward to 2011 when someone  purchased an original back to the future  delorean for 541 thousand dollars  thankfully deloreans that didn't appear  in the film are much more affordable a  1981 dmz 12 went for 23 100  at an auction in 2019  of course many delorean car collectors  don't just want a classic sports car  they want the time machine from back to  the future this led many fans to modify  their deloreans and make them resemble  doc brown's iconic design among these  builders are oliver and terry holler who  spent three and a half months refitting  a delorean sports car with scrap metal  and surplus electronics to recreate the  back to the future time machine today  the hollers volunteer for the michael j  fox foundation for parkinson's research  they aren't the only delorean fanatics  in the documentary back in time fan joe  waltzer recalled that he promised he  would buy a delorean and turn it into a  time machine today waltzer is on the  time machine restoration team and helped  restore one of the original delorean  time machines after it fell into  disrepair on the universal studios movie  lot  if you look closely at the dates on doc  brown's time machine you'll see that  marty mcfly first drove the time  traveling delorean on october 26 1985 in  the parking lot of twin pines mall which  was actually puente hills mall in city  of industry california however back to  the future was released to the public on  july 3 1985 almost four months before  the film's events took place  this led a group of fans to show up at  the puente hills mall on october 26 1985  to see if marty or doc brown would  appear in the famous delorean  unfortunately neither character made a  real life appearance but that didn't  stop another group of fans from showing  up at the puente hills mall again in  october 2015 to see if doc or marty  would suddenly appear 30 years later  this time the owner of a delorean time  machine replica was on location to give  fans a fun photo op  in the documentary back in time michael  j fox recalled that during the 1985  world premiere of back to the future he  was seated next to none other than  princess diana who was attending the  screening with her then husband prince  charles prior to the event fox and the  other attendees received a list of rules  for how they should interact with  british royalty among them they were  forbidden from turning their backs on  the prince or princess and could not  speak unless spoken to unfortunately  shortly after the movie began fox  realized he had to go to the bathroom  and found himself in an uncomfortable  position he couldn't walk away from  princess diana without turning his back  on her and he couldn't excuse himself  since he was instructed not to speak to  her  so the whole the whole thing was  i sat in total pain watching the movie  with the princess of wales and it was  great  it was i think she was smoking hot  before back to the future was officially  released on july 3rd 1985 a test  audience got to see the film when it  first screened in may of 1985 at the  century domes theater complex in san  jose california unlike a premiere there  were no signs or hints suggesting what  the movie would be about people did get  excited when the opening credits  revealed that the film was created by  steven spielberg and robert zemeckis but  many still had no idea what to expect  bob gale recalled years later when doc  brown sent his dog einstein forward in  time one minute causing him to vanish  some audience members were distressed  because they thought the dog had been  killed of course these viewers didn't  realize the film was a comedy  today when people think of back to the  future they think of the entire trilogy  to a contemporary audience it appears  that zemeckis and gayle always planned  the story to be an epic three-part tale  after all the infamous words to be  continued appeared at the end of the  first movie right except that for  audiences who saw the film in 1985 they  didn't the original flick did indeed end  with doc brown taking marty and his  girlfriend jennifer parker to the future  but neither zemeckis nor gayle  envisioned the movie as anything more  than a standalone however when the film  became a huge hit the studio put  pressure on the filmmakers to continue  the story as a result when back to the  future was released on home video in  1986 mca universal added the words to be  continued at the end  this helped build anticipation among  fans as well as new viewers who saw the  movie for the first time on vhs tape  which was helpful since back to the  future part 2 wouldn't hit theaters  until 1989.  in 2002 the 2b continued ending was  removed again when the back to the  future trilogy was released as a dvd box  set  back to the future might be considered a  sweet comedy by many fans but it does  have some uncomfortable moments  particularly the scenes between marty  mcfly and his teenage mother lorraine  after marty is hit by the car that was  supposed to strike his father lorraine  falls for him unaware that marty is  actually her own son it was this subplot  that caused the movie to be turned down  by disney when zemeckis and gail were  looking for a studio to produce the film  gail would later recall we went in to  meet with an executive and he says are  you guys nuts are you insane we can't  make a movie like this you've got the  kid and the mother in his car it's  incest this is disney it's too dirty for  us  weirdly the incest plot proved popular  with at least one audience member in the  documentary back in time adam f goldberg  creator of the goldbergs tv show  recalled that his mother came back from  the movie theater in 1985 and told him i  just saw this amazing movie called back  to the future it's about a boy who goes  back and falls in love with his mom  her review immediately turned off the  younger goldberg for obvious reasons  although he later came around and became  a fan of the film that is  at its core back to the future is a  movie about keeping families together  this motivated a young dan harmon  co-creator of the back to the future  influenced adult animated series rick  and morty to make his parents go see the  film because they were separated at the  time in the documentary back in time  harmon said subconsciously it was like  maybe my parents will get back together  if  if they watch this they did get back  together  as huey lewis famously sings on the back  to the future soundtrack that's the  power of love  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

